  "notes": "{鍛|きた}える originally meant to forge metal, but in modern Japanese it most commonly means to train or strengthen the body or mind.\n\nIchidan verb.\n- Negative: {鍛|きた}えない\n- Polite: {鍛|きた}えます\n- Te-form: {鍛|きた}えて\n- Past: {鍛|きた}えた\n- Passive: {鍛|きた}えられる\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {体|からだ}を{鍛|きた}える: to train one's body\n- {足腰|あしこし}を{鍛|きた}える: to strengthen one's legs and back\n- {精神|せいしん}を{鍛|きた}える: to discipline one's mind\n- {筋肉|きんにく}を{鍛|きた}える: to build muscle",
